  "id": "oceansoda-ethz-v2",
  "stac_version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "OceanSODA-ETHZv2 is a global, gap-filled data set of surface ocean CO2 fugacity (fCO2) and the associated sea-air CO2 flux (FCO2) at 8-day, 0.25° x 0.25° resolution, covering 1982-2022. It is produced with a combination of gradient-boosted decision trees and an ensemble of feed-forward neural networks trained on SOCAT v2023 shipboard fCO2 observations, using sea surface temperature, salinity, chlorophyll-a, mixed-layer depth, sea surface height and atmospheric CO2 as predictors. It supersedes the original monthly, 1°x1° OceanSODA-ETHZ product (Gregor & Gruber, 2021), improving the representation of fine-scale spatial gradients and subseasonal variability (e.g. upwelling filaments, mesoscale fronts, tropical/extratropical storms) while maintaining similar accuracy at the global scale.",
